---

---

<section class="status-quo">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="header">
            <h2 class="section-title">The "Standard" is Broken.</h2>
            <p class="section-subtitle">
                Turning Notion into a website shouldn't be a struggle. But for
                years, it's been a compromise of speed, reliability, and
                professionalism.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid">
            <div class="visual">
                <div class="card glitch-card">
                    <img
                        src="/landing/status-quo.png"
                        alt="Broken Notion Experience"
                        class="status-img"
                    />
                    <div class="noise"></div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="pain-points">
                <div class="pain-item">
                    <div class="icon">🔗</div>
                    <div class="text">
                        <h3>Domain Dilemma</h3>
                        <p>
                            Ugly UUIDs and "notion.site" subdomains don't scream
                            professional. Your blog's identity shouldn't feel
                            like a database entry.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="pain-item">
                    <div class="icon">🔄</div>
                    <div class="text">
                        <h3>The Infinite Spinner</h3>
                        <p>
                            Waiting 4 seconds for a single page to hydrate. In
                            the age of instant feedback, your audience has
                            already closed the tab.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="pain-item">
                    <div class="icon">❌</div>
                    <div class="text">
                        <h3>Image Link Anxiety</h3>
                        <p>
                            Checking your own portfolio only to find dead AWS
                            links. Notion's expiring images shouldn't be your
                            problem.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<style>
    .status-quo {
        padding: 8rem 0;
        background: hsl(var(--background));
    }

    .header {
        text-align: center;
        max-width: 800px;
        margin: 0 auto 5rem;
    }

    .section-title {
        font-size: 3.5rem;
        font-weight: 800;
        margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }

    .section-subtitle {
        font-size: 1.25rem;
        color: hsl(var(--muted-foreground));
    }

    .grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
        gap: 5rem;
        align-items: center;
    }

    .visual {
        position: relative;
    }

    .glitch-card {
        background: #000;
        border-radius: 20px;
        overflow: hidden;
        border: 1px solid hsl(0 100% 50% / 0.2);
        box-shadow: 0 0 50px -10px hsl(0 100% 50% / 0.1);
    }

    .status-img {
        width: 100%;
        display: block;
        opacity: 0.8;
    }

    .pain-points {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 3rem;
    }

    .pain-item {
        display: flex;
        gap: 1.5rem;
    }

    .pain-item .icon {
        font-size: 2rem;
        flex-shrink: 0;
    }

    .pain-item h3 {
        font-size: 1.5rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .pain-item p {
        color: hsl(var(--muted-foreground));
        line-height: 1.6;
    }

    @media (max-width: 1024px) {
        .grid {
            grid-template-columns: 1fr;
            gap: 4rem;
        }
        .visual {
            order: 2;
        }
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
        .status-quo {
            padding: 5rem 0;
        }
        .section-title {
            font-size: 2.5rem;
        }
        .header {
            margin-bottom: 3rem;
        }
    }

    @media (max-width: 640px) {
        .status-quo {
            padding: 3.5rem 0;
        }
        .section-title {
            font-size: 2rem;
        }
        .pain-item h3 {
            font-size: 1.25rem;
        }
    }
</style>
